 10: - When a catalogue maps individual designs on an album page to source plates, state which side it assigns to which number and read the source-plate description too; do not let a silhouette resemblance stand in for a motif match. Page 3 of the Cruycen album. Provisional.
 11: - When a collection record gives no description, stay with its title and visible surface before supplying a use for the object. The pilaster fragment's lower field. Provisional.
